Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63836,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7e3db74b61ef0a00e61117154ecf402d","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; I kinda feel bad for the ppl on the \"do not tip list\". However, we are spending more than enough money on everything so this list is extremely helpful.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1530033,"PostDate":1317832148,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I kinda feel bad for the ppl on the \"do not tip list\". However, we are spending more than enough money on everything so this list is extremely helpful.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ckwlualum@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1310763377,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-242380.JPG?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"meBonidie2be","Id":242380,"Name":"meBonidie2be","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63836,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d0f847883daceff8f3d79fd2a8d97f43","RawContent":"The list was helpful. Thanks for sharing that info. Where did you find it?  \n \n I was prepared to tip everyone too!! I&#039;ll have to discuss with fiance and see what he thinks. But the point about the photographer makes sense!  \n \n [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]Sllefebvr[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n I know.. I would of tipped everybody.. but obv. we don&#039;t need to which is nice to know!! I can keep that money in my own pocket!![\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1530059,"PostDate":1317835607,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> The list was helpful. Thanks for sharing that info. Where did you find it?\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I was prepared to tip everyone too!! I'll have to discuss with fiance and see what he thinks. But the point about the photographer makes sense!\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>Sllefebvr<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" style=\"border: 0px solid;\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> I know.. I would of tipped everybody.. but obv. we don't need to which is nice to know!! I can keep that money in my own pocket!!<\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"euneeq@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1292626164,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-234669.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Pucca","Id":234669,"Name":"Pucca","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63836,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"34255149b0f710be1ee0aaa9e5541489","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Very helpful - thank you!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1530306,"PostDate":1317858431,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Very helpful - thank you!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><p><span>Brad & Janine - November 10th, 2011.<\/span><br><span>Valentin Imperial Maya, Riviera Maya<\/span><br><span>Bride & Groom + 29<\/span><\/p><span><\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"janine_bolton@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1282608738,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-231642.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"JBean","Id":231642,"Name":"JBean","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63836,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"63ae734ee461f6e8a03ff97477fd05bb","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Thanks for the help.. I will set ahead budgets for tipping xxx&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1530527,"PostDate":1317898703,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Thanks for the help.. I will set ahead budgets for tipping xxx<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"jmbarroccu@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1315577866,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-245108.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":139,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"jennaba3","Id":245108,"Name":"jennaba3","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63836,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"1fab61647ccc9029e0658be8e25247c8","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Fantastic. Thank you so much!!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I am still wondering how much to tip our Event Planner. She works for the resort...I really have no idea how much her fee is. She will be on site during the wedding and has been phenomenal at working with me via email.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Anyone have any ideas on how much to tip her??&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1530621,"PostDate":1317918088,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Fantastic. Thank you so much!!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I am still wondering how much to tip our Event Planner. She works for the resort...I really have no idea how much her fee is. She will be on site during the wedding and has been phenomenal at working with me via email.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Anyone have any ideas on how much to tip her??<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"alucy20@excite.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1276902653,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-229322.JPG?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"lucy<3woody","Id":229322,"Name":"lucy<3woody","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63836,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7b7d48edd8c677ec767d1e10ff02b32c","RawContent":"This is very informative.  What about a travel agent who helps with the travel arrangements for you and your guests?\n   [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]Sllefebvr[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Here girls I did some research on destination weddings and here was the best result \n [list]\n[*]You do not need to tip your florist unless he\/she does something spectacular or really out-of-the-floral-realm for you. If he tracks down the filling for your goody bags, or she blows your mind with something you weren\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t expecting, by all means, feel free to tip the florist. But it isn\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t something you need to build into your budget.\n[*]You don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t need to tip your caterer, but you will need to tip the servers and bartenders. If you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t have a wedding planner to guide you, ask the caterer what\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s appropriate per person.\n[*]Don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t tip the photographer. If you adored her, order more prints!\n[*]Don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t tip the wedding cake baker.\n[*]Don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t tip a band, unless they stay extra time and don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t bill you for it.\n[*]Tip a DJ if he\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s really, really good. $50 is more than enough.\n[*]If you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re staying in a small hotel and you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve taken over the whole place for your wedding, be sure to tip the hotel manager\/concierge who has helped you with everything. You should also tip the breakfast or housekeeping staff, but you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t need to do it individually. Give a tip to the person in charge of that staff and ask them to split it with the people who worked during your wedding.\n[*]If you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re staying at a villa or private property with a house manager or caretaker, tip if you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re having the reception on the property and the person is being very helpful. Remember, the property owners made money on you. The caretaker or property manager is on salary and had to put up with you because it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s part of his job. If they do a great job, acknowledge it. If you have daily maid service, it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s appropriate to leave a tip of $2-$5 per day in your room. If you have a 5-bedroom house, you should tip $10 per day at the end of your stay if they did a good job.\n[*]Do not tip your wedding officiant.\n[*]Do not tip your rental equipment delivery guys \u00e2\u20ac\u201d you paid a delivery fee already.\n[*]Finally, do tip your wedding planner. As self-serving as this may sound, I get asked this question a lot so I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122m going to tackle it openly and honestly.\n[\/list] If you have a good wedding planner who is charging you a reasonable fee and isn\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t marking up your services, you should tip her at the end of your wedding if you are happy with her services. When deciding how much to tip, think about how much her total fee was, and think about how much money she saved you (there will be items that stick out when you think about it), and how challenging you may have been as a client. If you know you drove her nuts or were very demanding (and she was nice about it), compensate her for the extra time and effort she had to put in to your big day. Tip between 15 and 20 percent of her wedding fee. To some extend it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s like a restaurant, if you were satisfied, go 15 percent. If you were thrilled and she did a great job for you, go 20 percent or more. If you felt like she dropped the ball, give her 10 percent, or don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t tip her at all. A tip is supposed to be a gratuity for a job well done, whether it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s a waitress, a hairdresser or a wedding planner. \n The exception to the rule is the wedding planner who asks for a tip. That is just so gauche. Sometimes I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ll make a joke about it to my clients when they\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re really super impressed with something I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve done. When they\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re telling me how great I am or how much money I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve saved them, I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ll make some joke like \u00e2\u20ac\u0153remember that when it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s time to tip me,\u00e2\u20ac\u009d or something like that. But I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve never ever told a bride up front that a tip was required, or asked a bride for a gratuity after the wedding. Some brides are just thoughtful. I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve received lovely thank-you gifts and even sweeter notes \u00e2\u20ac\u201d and those can be very rewarding as well. \n If you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t use a wedding planner and a banquet manager or someone else from the hotel steps into that role for your wedding, be prepared to tip her at the end of the event as long as everything has gone smoothly. She is your de facto wedding planner and you should thank her for executing that role well. It doesn\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t need to be as much as you would tip a wedding planner, but a token to let her know her work was appreciated is more than appropriate. \n So when your wedding planner gives you the list of tips you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ll need for your wedding a few weeks before the big day, take a moment to think about whether you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ll want to have some extra on hand to tip your planner too, assuming she delivers all that she promised on your wedding day. If in the end she doesn\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t deserve it, spend it on a spa day on your honeymoon.[\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1531585,"PostDate":1318124417,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> This is very informative. \u00a0What about a travel agent who helps with the travel arrangements for you and your guests?<br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>Sllefebvr<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" style=\"border: 0px solid;\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Here girls I did some research on destination weddings and here was the best result<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <ul> <li> You do not need to tip your florist unless he\/she does something spectacular or really out-of-the-floral-realm for you. If he tracks down the filling for your goody bags, or she blows your mind with something you weren\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t expecting, by all means, feel free to tip the florist. But it isn\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t something you need to build into your budget.<\/li> <li> You don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t need to tip your caterer, but you will need to tip the servers and bartenders. If you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t have a wedding planner to guide you, ask the caterer what\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s appropriate per person.<\/li> <li> Don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t tip the photographer. If you adored her, order more prints!<\/li> <li> Don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t tip the wedding cake baker.<\/li> <li> Don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t tip a band, unless they stay extra time and don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t bill you for it.<\/li> <li> Tip a DJ if he\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s really, really good. $50 is more than enough.<\/li> <li> If you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re staying in a small hotel and you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve taken over the whole place for your wedding, be sure to tip the hotel manager\/concierge who has helped you with everything. You should also tip the breakfast or housekeeping staff, but you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t need to do it individually. Give a tip to the person in charge of that staff and ask them to split it with the people who worked during your wedding.<\/li> <li> If you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re staying at a villa or private property with a house manager or caretaker, tip if you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re having the reception on the property and the person is being very helpful. Remember, the property owners made money on you. The caretaker or property manager is on salary and had to put up with you because it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s part of his job. If they do a great job, acknowledge it. If you have daily maid service, it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s appropriate to leave a tip of $2-$5 per day in your room. If you have a 5-bedroom house, you should tip $10 per day at the end of your stay if they did a good job.<\/li> <li> Do not tip your wedding officiant.<\/li> <li> Do not tip your rental equipment delivery guys \u00e2\u20ac\u201d you paid a delivery fee already.<\/li> <li> Finally, do tip your wedding planner. As self-serving as this may sound, I get asked this question a lot so I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122m going to tackle it openly and honestly.<\/li> <\/ul> <p> If you have a good wedding planner who is charging you a reasonable fee and isn\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t marking up your services, you should tip her at the end of your wedding if you are happy with her services. When deciding how much to tip, think about how much her total fee was, and think about how much money she saved you (there will be items that stick out when you think about it), and how challenging you may have been as a client. If you know you drove her nuts or were very demanding (and she was nice about it), compensate her for the extra time and effort she had to put in to your big day. Tip between 15 and 20 percent of her wedding fee. To some extend it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s like a restaurant, if you were satisfied, go 15 percent. If you were thrilled and she did a great job for you, go 20 percent or more. If you felt like she dropped the ball, give her 10 percent, or don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t tip her at all. A tip is supposed to be a gratuity for a job well done, whether it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s a waitress, a hairdresser or a wedding planner.<\/p> <p> The exception to the rule is the wedding planner who asks for a tip. That is just so gauche. Sometimes I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ll make a joke about it to my clients when they\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re really super impressed with something I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve done. When they\u00e2\u20ac\u2122re telling me how great I am or how much money I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve saved them, I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ll make some joke like \u00e2\u20ac\u0153remember that when it\u00e2\u20ac\u2122s time to tip me,\u00e2\u20ac\u009d or something like that. But I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve never ever told a bride up front that a tip was required, or asked a bride for a gratuity after the wedding. Some brides are just thoughtful. I\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ve received lovely thank-you gifts and even sweeter notes \u00e2\u20ac\u201d and those can be very rewarding as well.<\/p> <p> If you don\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t use a wedding planner and a banquet manager or someone else from the hotel steps into that role for your wedding, be prepared to tip her at the end of the event as long as everything has gone smoothly. She is your de facto wedding planner and you should thank her for executing that role well. It doesn\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t need to be as much as you would tip a wedding planner, but a token to let her know her work was appreciated is more than appropriate.<\/p> <p> So when your wedding planner gives you the list of tips you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ll need for your wedding a few weeks before the big day, take a moment to think about whether you\u00e2\u20ac\u2122ll want to have some extra on hand to tip your planner too, assuming she delivers all that she promised on your wedding day. If in the end she doesn\u00e2\u20ac\u2122t deserve it, spend it on a spa day on your honeymoon.<\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"deeliight40@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1316322716,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-245472.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":116,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"dshane","Id":245472,"Name":"dshane","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63836,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"a57a0d234bd64afa53ecc3f7b1f810e0","RawContent":"I know some ladies have had great experiences with their travel agents but mine on the other hand...not so much.  I have two people working on my wedding group contract and they seem to mess up so much stuff, don&#039;t get things right, contact the wrong people, never contact me with updates or deadlines, I always have to ask for a re-cap and then tell them where they messed up and so much more.  There is no way they are getting anything but a thank you card with a wedding picture in it. \n   [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]dshane[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n This is very informative.  What about a travel agent who helps with the travel arrangements for you and your guests?  \n[\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1532069,"PostDate":1318265263,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I know some ladies have had great experiences with their travel agents but mine on the other hand...not so much.\u00a0 I have two people working on my wedding group contract and they seem to mess up so much stuff, don't get things right, contact the wrong people, never contact me with updates or deadlines, I always have to ask for a re-cap and then tell them where they messed up and so much more.\u00a0 There is no way they are getting anything but a thank you card with a wedding picture in it.\u00a0<br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>dshane<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" style=\"border: 0px solid;\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> This is very informative. \u00a0What about a travel agent who helps with the travel arrangements for you and your guests?\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"sxctaz18@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1279757050,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-230504.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":123,"PhotoHeight":160,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"sxcT","Id":230504,"Name":"sxcT","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63836,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"a8a6570a755715d45c52e9568adc9787","RawContent":"I know what you mean...I wouldn&#039;t even send that to them! \n   [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]sxcT[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n I know some ladies have had great experiences with their travel agents but mine on the other hand...not so much.  I have two people working on my wedding group contract and they seem to mess up so much stuff, don&#039;t get things right, contact the wrong people, never contact me with updates or deadlines, I always have to ask for a re-cap and then tell them where they messed up and so much more.  There is no way they are getting anything but a thank you card with a wedding picture in it.   \n[\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1532139,"PostDate":1318273414,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I know what you mean...I wouldn't even send that to them!\u00a0<br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>sxcT<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" style=\"border: 0px solid;\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> I know some ladies have had great experiences with their travel agents but mine on the other hand...not so much.\u00a0 I have two people working on my wedding group contract and they seem to mess up so much stuff, don't get things right, contact the wrong people, never contact me with updates or deadlines, I always have to ask for a re-cap and then tell them where they messed up and so much more.\u00a0 There is no way they are getting anything but a thank you card with a wedding picture in it.\u00a0\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"ssanzick@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1295388669,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-235711.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Sharon99","Id":235711,"Name":"Sharon99","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63836,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"76e5c8bfc8cc49382e6012c24e7b77fa","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Hey,&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Thanks for the post.&amp;nbsp; I hadn&#039;t even thought about tipping, but it completely makes sense.&amp;nbsp; It&#039;s just something that slipped my mind.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I read the bottom part, about tipping the wedding planner.&amp;nbsp; Our hotel is providing a wedding planner for us, but correspondence with her is minimal.&amp;nbsp; How much should we tip her?&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Thanks,&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1533431,"PostDate":1318477213,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Hey,<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Thanks for the post.\u00a0 I hadn't even thought about tipping, but it completely makes sense.\u00a0 It's just something that slipped my mind.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I read the bottom part, about tipping the wedding planner.\u00a0 Our hotel is providing a wedding planner for us, but correspondence with her is minimal.\u00a0 How much should we tip her?<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Thanks,<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"erica.bowley@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1304468686,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-239601.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"FranticBride2be","Id":239601,"Name":"FranticBride2be","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":63836,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"d344fa9632817b5176007d8e9775b571","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; I have a bit of a different guideline for tipping - if someone is running their own business (ie. the florist is the owner of the shop, or the person who does your hair runs their own business) you don&#039;t tip them, since they have set their own prices to incorporate this. If they are working for someone else and being paid a salary or hourly wage, then it is appropriate to consider tipping. Sometimes it might be hard to tell, especially at a DW, but that&#039;s my general rule for tips. The lady who does my nails works out of her home and sets her own prices, so no tipping. If I get them done at a salon or spa, I do tip though.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Hope that helps some people!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1533568,"PostDate":1318522341,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I have a bit of a different guideline for tipping - if someone is running their own business (ie. the florist is the owner of the shop, or the person who does your hair runs their own business) you don't tip them, since they have set their own prices to incorporate this. If they are working for someone else and being paid a salary or hourly wage, then it is appropriate to consider tipping. Sometimes it might be hard to tell, especially at a DW, but that's my general rule for tips. The lady who does my nails works out of her home and sets her own prices, so no tipping. If I get them done at a salon or spa, I do tip though.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Hope that helps some people!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"cdctt@shaw.ca","IpAddress":"","GroupId":47,"GroupName":"Site Supporter","JoinDate":1293685168,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-234899.JPG?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"all the love","Id":234899,"Name":"all the love","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":106,"TotalPages":11,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":20,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":100},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
